====================================================================================================================
RUNG 1 -- galaxies: eta from the KiDS-1000 stacked lensing RAR (on disk, a real Delta-Sigma stack)
====================================================================================================================
  isolated KiDS-bright lenses: 15 acceleration bins, g_bar = 1.38e-15 to 3.92e-12 m/s^2
  canonical  stars only     : eta = 1.41 +- 0.03 over all 15 bins; 1.51 +- 0.04 over the 12 deep bins (g_bar < 1e-12, x < 0.011)
  canonical  stars + hot gas: eta = 0.89 +- 0.02 over all 15 bins; 0.86 +- 0.02 over the 12 deep bins (g_bar < 1e-12, x < 0.011)
  alt        stars only     : eta = 1.29 +- 0.03 over all 15 bins; 1.38 +- 0.03 over the 12 deep bins (g_bar < 1e-12, x < 0.011)
  alt        stars + hot gas: eta = 0.81 +- 0.02 over all 15 bins; 0.78 +- 0.02 over the 12 deep bins (g_bar < 1e-12, x < 0.011)
  the galaxy rung is therefore eta = 0.81 to 1.41: the spread is the BARYON BUDGET (whether the hot gas around
  isolated galaxies is counted), not the statistics, exactly as it will be for the groups below.
  [PASS] 55-1 the ladder starts at 1: the KiDS-1000 stacked lensing of isolated galaxies brackets eta = 1 between its two baryon budgets on both footings, so any rise measured further up the ladder is a real rise and not an offset in the zero point   (eta(galaxies) = 1.41 +- 0.03 with stars alone and 0.89 with Brouwer's hot-gas correction (canonical); 1.29 / 0.81 (alt).  The 0.15-0.25 dex stellar M/L systematic on g_bar -- this repository's own items 2, 65 and 66 -- is far larger than the 0.03 statistical error, so this is a consistency, not a measurement)

