====================================================================================================================
the estimator's own weakness: mass and redshift are confounded in a flux-selected sample
====================================================================================================================
  corr(log M500, z) = +0.393 in the clean sample -- groups are nearby, clusters are far, so a mass trend and a
  redshift trend cannot be separated without care.  The fits above already carry a linear z term.  Now the low-z cut:
